    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76564" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδά̆ρ-ιον</span></b> , τό, 
			Dim. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παῖς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>little boy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				494
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pl.</u>
				536
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ παιδαρίου</span> from
				<i>a child</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				207d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ μικροῦ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					53.19
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. εἶ</span> you're <i>a mere
				boy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				821
			</span></i>; also, <i>little girl</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1203
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				164
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				428
			</span></i> (in this sense only 
				Att.
			 acc. to Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.321
			</span></i> P.): in pl., <i>young children</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				568
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. καὶ γύναια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					1.130
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.305
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>young slave</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				823
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				843
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
